c QIF benchmark 5/7: partial bit-mask leak. l = h AND 0b0011.
c
c Vars: 1..4 = h1 (LSB) .. h4 (MSB), secret 4-bit value.
c        5 = l1, 6 = l2 — observable bottom-2 bits (l = h AND mask).
c Logic: l1 <-> h1, l2 <-> h2. Bits h3, h4 are unconstrained
c (perfectly secret); bits h1, h2 are perfectly leaked.
c Models: 16 (4 secret bits, observables forced).
c Leakage: 2 bits of 4 = 50% disclosure.
c
c Reference: Koepf & Basin, "An Information-Theoretic Model for
c Adaptive Side-Channel Attacks", CCS 2007 — masking partial-leak
c canonical example.
p cnf 6 4
-5 1 0
5 -1 0
-6 2 0
6 -2 0
